{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 969 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "e869188fe8662dbfb57e6e8ec59f70ac7c54a4db04945202d125d5fb2fdab5ac" :edb/db-before-t 968 :edb/db-after-t 969 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534281 50 #inst "2026-10-06T15:30:38.691Z" 13194139534281 true] [17592186100630 1100 "Expand ${( 3x + y )}^3$ using the binomial theorem." 13194139534281 true] [17592186100630 1100 "Expand ${(3x + y)}^3$ using the binomial theorem." 13194139534281 false] [17592186100630 1145 "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n$, we have\n\n$$\n{(a + b)^n} = {n \\choose 0}{a^n}{b^0} + {n \\choose 1}{a^{n - 1}}{b^1} + {n \\choose 2}{a^{n - 2}}{b^2} + \\cdots + {n \\choose n}{a^0}{b^n}\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(3x +y)}^3$, we have $a=3x$, $b=y$, and $n=3$.\n\nTherefore, we can expand ${(3x + y)}^3$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(3x + y)^{3} &= (\\frac{3}{0})(3x)^{3}(y)^{0} + (\\frac{3}{1})(3x)^{3 - 1}(y)^{1} + (\\frac{3}{2})(3x)^{3 - 2}(y)^{2} + (\\frac{3}{3})(3x)^{3 - 3}(y)^{3} \\\\\n&= (\\frac{3}{0})(3x)^{3}(1) + (\\frac{3}{1})(3x)^{2}(y)^{1} + (\\frac{3}{2})(3x)^{1}(y)^{2} + (\\frac{3}{3})(3x)^{0}(y)^{3} \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot (3x)^{3} + 3 \\cdot (3x)^{2}(y) + 3 \\cdot (3x)(y)^{2} + 1 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (y^{3}) \\\\\n&= 27x^{3} + 27x^{2}y + 9xy^{2} + y^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534281 false] [17592186100630 1145 "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n{(a + b)^n} = {n \\choose 0}{a^n}{b^0} + {n \\choose 1}{a^{n - 1}}{b^1} + {n \\choose 2}{a^{n - 2}}{b^2} +  \\cdots  + {n \\choose n}{a^0}{b^n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(3x +y)}^3,$ we have  $a=3x,$ $b=y,$ and $n=3.$ \n\nTherefore, we can expand ${(3x + y)}^3$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3x+y)^{3} & =(\\frac{3}{0})(3x)^{3}(y)^{0}+(\\frac{3}{1})(3x)^{3-1}(y)^{1}+(\\frac{3}{2})(3x)^{3-2}(y)^{2}+(\\frac{3}{3})(3x)^{3-3}(y)^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{0})(3x)^{3}(1)+(\\frac{3}{1})(3x)^{2}(y)^{1}+(\\frac{3}{2})(3x)^{1}(y)^{2}+(\\frac{3}{3})(3x)^{0}(y)^{3} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (3x)^{3}+3\\cdot (3x)^{2}(y)+3\\cdot (3x)(y)^{2}+1\\cdot 1\\cdot ({y}^{3}) \\\\  & =27{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}y+9x{y}^{2}+{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534281 true] [17592186100631 1100 "Find the coefficient of $x^{4}$ in the expansion of ${\\left( {3 + x} \\right)^{7}} .$" 13194139534281 true] [17592186100631 1100 "Find the coefficient of $x^{4}$ in the expansion of ${\\left({3 + x} \\right)^{7}}$." 13194139534281 false] [17592186100631 1145 "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n$, we have\n\n$$\n{(a + b)^n} = {n \\choose 0}{a^n}{b^0} + {n \\choose 1}{a^{n - 1}}{b^1} + {n \\choose 2}{a^{n - 2}}{b^2} + \\cdots + {n \\choose n}{a^0}{b^n}\n$$\n\nIn the case of\n\n$$\n{\\left({3 +x} \\right)^{7}}\n$$\n\nwe have $a=3$, $b=x$, and $n=7$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n(3 + x)^{7} = (\\frac{7}{0})3^{7}x^{0} + (\\frac{7}{1})3^{7 - 1}x^{1} + (\\frac{7}{2})3^{7 - 2}x^{2} + ⋯ + (\\frac{7}{7})3^{7 - 7}x^{7}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the $x^4$ term must be\n\n$$\n{7 \\choose 4}{3^{7 - 4}}{x^4}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the coefficient, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(\\frac{7}{4})3^{7 - 4} &= 35 \\cdot 3^{3} \\\\\n&= 35 \\cdot 27 \\\\\n&= 945\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of $x^{4}$ is $945$." 13194139534281 false] [17592186100631 1145 "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n{(a + b)^n} = {n \\choose 0}{a^n}{b^0} + {n \\choose 1}{a^{n - 1}}{b^1} + {n \\choose 2}{a^{n - 2}}{b^2} +  \\cdots  + {n \\choose n}{a^0}{b^n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${\\left( {3 +x} \\right)^{7}},$ we have $a=3,$ $b=x,$ and $n=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+x)^{7}=(\\frac{7}{0}){3}^{7}{x}^{0}+(\\frac{7}{1}){3}^{7-1}{x}^{1}+(\\frac{7}{2}){3}^{7-2}{x}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{7}{7}){3}^{7-7}{x}^{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the $x^4$ term must be\n\n$$\n{7 \\choose 4}{3^{7 - 4}}{x^4}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating the coefficient, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{7}{4}){3}^{7-4} & =35\\cdot {3}^{3} \\\\  & =35\\cdot 27 \\\\  & =945.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of $x^{4}$ is $945.$" 13194139534281 true] [17592186100709 1100 "Find the first three terms of the binomial expansion of ${( x - 3y )}^ 5.$" 13194139534281 true] [17592186100709 1100 "Find the first three terms of the binomial expansion of ${(x - 3y)}^ 5$." 13194139534281 false] [17592186100709 1145 "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n$, we have\n\n$$\n{(a + b)^n} = {n \\choose 0}{a^n}{b^0} + {n \\choose 1}{a^{n - 1}}{b^1} + {n \\choose 2}{a^{n - 2}}{b^2} + \\cdots + {n \\choose n}{a^0}{b^n}\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(x - 3y)}^ 5$, we have $a=x$, $b=-3y$, and $n=5$.\n\nTherefore, the first three terms of ${(x - 3y)}^ 5$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 3y)^{5} &= (\\frac{5}{0})(x)^{5}(-3y)^{0} + (\\frac{5}{1})(x)^{5 - 1}(-3y)^{1} + (\\frac{5}{2})(x)^{5 - 2}(-3y)^{2} + ⋯ \\\\\n&= 1(x)^{5} + 5(x)^{4}(-3y) + 10(x)^{3}(9y^{2}) + ⋯ \\\\\n&= x^{5} - 15x^{4}y + 90x^{3}y^{2} + ⋯\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534281 false] [17592186100709 1145 "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n{(a + b)^n} = {n \\choose 0}{a^n}{b^0} + {n \\choose 1}{a^{n - 1}}{b^1} + {n \\choose 2}{a^{n - 2}}{b^2} +  \\cdots  + {n \\choose n}{a^0}{b^n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(x - 3y)}^ 5,$ we have  $a=x,$ $b=-3y ,$ and $n=5.$ \n\nTherefore, the first three terms of ${(x - 3y)}^ 5$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3y)^{5} & =(\\frac{5}{0})(x)^{5}(-3y)^{0}+(\\frac{5}{1})(x)^{5-1}(-3y)^{1}+(\\frac{5}{2})(x)^{5-2}(-3y)^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =1(x)^{5}+5(x)^{4}(-3y)+10(x)^{3}(9{y}^{2})+⋯ \\\\  & ={x}^{5}-15{x}^{4}y+90{x}^{3}{y}^{2}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534281 true] [17592186100804 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283127 13194139534281 true] [17592186100804 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283134 13194139534281 true] [17592186100804 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283141 13194139534281 true] [17592186100804 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283148 13194139534281 true] [17592186100805 1020 #edb/ref 1759218